-<div class="board" aria-label="Illustrative replenishment review" data-aria-en="Illustrative replenishment review" data-aria-zh="补货核对示例"><div class="board-inner"><div class="board-top"><div><span class="micro">TOMORROW’S PREPARATION</span><strong>Ready for your review</strong></div><span class="pill">Illustrative demo</span></div><div class="context"><div>Weather context<b>Rain may change demand</b></div><div>Calendar context<b>Check local holidays</b></div></div><table class="demo-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Ingredient</th><th scope="col">Suggested packs</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Fresh milk</td><td><b>15 boxes</b></td></tr><tr><td>Oat milk</td><td><b>7 cartons</b></td></tr><tr><td>Coffee beans</td><td><b>3 bags</b></td></tr></tbody></table><div class="board-note">Review quantities → Approve the list → Create supplier drafts<br>Example quantities only. No live purchasing takes place on this website.</div></div></div></section>
-<div class="wrap band"><span>Weather &amp; holiday context</span><span>Owner review before procurement</span><span>Supplier drafts, ready to check</span></div>
-<section id="workflow" class="wrap section"><p class="eyebrow">From closing time to opening time</p><h2>Four steps. One considered<br>decision.</h2><div class="steps"><article><span class="step-num">01</span><h3>Understand tomorrow</h3><p>The local app combines demo sales, stock, recipes and selected weather and holiday context to estimate demand.</p></article><article><span class="step-num">02</span><h3>Review the shopping list</h3><p>Ingredients are converted into purchasable packs. The owner can adjust quantities and inspect any resulting shortfall.</p></article><article><span class="step-num">03</span><h3>Approve with confidence</h3><p>The owner confirms the list in the local or phone workbench. Approval creates a recorded procurement draft.</p></article><article><span class="step-num">04</span><h3>Prepare supplier drafts</h3><p>With optional Gmail authorization, approved drafts can be saved in the owner’s Gmail drafts folder. The owner decides whether to send.</p></article></div></section>
-<section class="data-section"><div class="wrap section split"><div><p class="eyebrow">Clear boundaries for your data</p><h2>Your workbench stays<br>on your computer.</h2><p>This public website explains the project. The replenishment workbench, purchasing records and Google authorization credentials are managed by the locally installed application.</p><p>Google authorization begins from that local workbench. This site has no token-entry form, sales-data upload or procurement controls.</p><a class="text-link" href="/privacy/">Read the complete privacy policy →</a></div><ul class="data-list"><li><span>↗</span><div><strong>Gmail is optional</strong><p>Connect your own account to save approved procurement drafts. Access tokens can refresh when needed.</p></div></li><li><span>✓</span><div><strong>Only the necessary Google permission</strong><p>The app requests gmail.compose. Google defines this as managing drafts and sending email; this implementation creates drafts and checks connectivity.</p></div></li><li><span>↶</span><div><strong>You can disconnect</strong><p>Clear local authorization in the workbench or revoke access in your Google Account. Existing Gmail drafts remain until you delete them.</p></div></li></ul></div></section>
-<section class="wrap index-note"><div><h3>A demonstration, with honest limits.</h3><p>Sales and inventory examples are synthetic. Forecast accuracy for a real café has not been validated. Weather data and optional cloud inference require their respective services; owner approval remains essential.</p></div><div lang="zh-CN"><h3>明日备货，让收店前的决定更清楚。</h3><p>在本机工作台查看天气与假日影响，按包装修改采购量，确认后生成供应商草稿。公开网站用于项目介绍和政策披露；演示采用模拟数据，采购由老板最终决定。</p></div></section></main>'''
