-terms = f'''<p class="doc-intro">These terms describe the intended use and practical limits of the Cafe Replenishment demonstration and its informational website.</p><p class="updated">Effective date: 22 October 2026 · Application: Cafe Replenishment</p>
-<h2 id="purpose">1. Intended use</h2><p>Cafe Replenishment is an independently maintained software demonstration for forecasting café demand, reviewing replenishment quantities and preparing supplier drafts. It currently uses synthetic demonstration sales and stock records. It is not a validated production inventory, accounting or purchasing service.</p>
-<h2 id="review">2. Owner review and purchasing</h2><p>The owner is responsible for verifying stock counts, recipes, units, pack sizes, supplier details, prices, delivery arrangements and expiry dates before purchasing. Forecasts, weather context and holiday effects are estimates. They do not guarantee future demand, ingredient availability, cost savings or business outcomes.</p><p>Approving a list creates procurement records and local supplier drafts. Saving to Gmail creates a draft, not a supplier order or payment. Opening a WhatsApp prefilled link does not establish that a message was sent or a supplier accepted an order.</p>
-<h2 id="accounts">3. Accounts, credentials and services</h2><p>Use only accounts and service credentials you are authorized to use. The application’s Google connection is optional and requires your consent. You are responsible for access to the local computer and workbench and for protecting service credentials. Never publish access tokens, refresh tokens, client secrets or the private runtime directory.</p><p>Google, Runpod, weather and messaging services may have their own terms, quotas, availability limits and fees. Optional Runpod inference may incur charges. This website does not purchase domains, compute capacity, ingredients or supplier services on your behalf.</p>
-<h2 id="availability">4. Availability and limitations</h2><p>The demonstration is provided as available, without a promise of uninterrupted service, forecast accuracy or suitability for a particular shop. Review outputs before relying on them. Local scheduled checks require the application’s server to remain running. A website deployment or Gmail connection does not itself validate the forecasting model.</p>
-<h2 id="privacy">5. Privacy and access control</h2><p>Read the <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a> before connecting Google or another service. The public website is separate from the local workbench and does not expose your inventory, approval records or OAuth credentials. Disconnecting an integration does not erase existing procurement records or Gmail drafts.</p>
-<h2 id="responsible-use">6. Responsible use and changes</h2><p>Do not use the application to access another person’s account without permission, evade service restrictions or send unwanted messages. The project may change or discontinue features. These terms do not override rights or obligations that cannot be excluded under applicable law.</p>
-<h2 id="contact">7. Contact</h2><p>{CONTACT}</p><div class="notice" lang="zh-CN">中文摘要：这是使用模拟数据的补货演示。老板需核对实际库存、供应商和采购条件；预测不保证真实经营效果。审批和生成草稿均不代表已下单、已发送或已付款。第三方服务可能产生费用。</div>'''
